/*  parserTest -- THE LIVE PARSER INCANTATION'S OWN POP. Tony, ruled 2026-09-17.

    `IncantForms/WorkingOn/parser` became definitions-only so `utilities` could include it;
    this is where those definitions are measured. It drives the LIVE `parser` -- the one
    every first-use install now resolves -- across four roots.

    ⚠ IT DOES NOT GATHER anyOrNumT's OR trigDO's CALLS, AND THE REASON IS A CORRECTION.
    Those two carry their OWN COMPLETE FROZEN COPIES of the incantation -- generateParse,
    walkRules, compileRules, parser -- by design. anyOrNumT's header says so in terms:
    "IncantForms/WorkingOn/parser, frozen, rooted at ANYorNum, with every gate ON and no
    probe scaffolding of any kind." They never called the shared definitions, so there was
    nothing of theirs to gather. What they needed was for their frozen names to stop
    COLLIDING with the live ones, which is a rename, not a move. Their roots are covered
    here against the LIVE copy, which is new coverage rather than relocated coverage.

    ⚠⚠ NO ROW CARRIES A PINNED ANSWER, DELIBERATELY. Two of these four roots have never run
    at all -- CASE 2 was dead code behind a second stop() in the source file, and the live
    parser has never been driven at ANYorNum or Start. Pinning a number that has never been
    produced is inventing a target, and a target regenerated green is not a target. What is
    asserted is only that the run REACHES ITS FOOT: each case prints a marker, the foot
    prints a sentinel, and the rows count markers. The values come when Tony has read them.

    ⚠ AND THE SENTINEL IS THE ONLY COMPLETENESS CLAIM THIS FILE MAKES. A case that hangs or
    dies takes the sentinel with it, which is the fact worth having first.  */
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(utilities);
search reset stack Grokking;
search GroupFields UnitTests Utilities list;

cerr "PT-1 parser(Search)":;
parser(Search);
Search("search list;");

cerr "PT-2 parser(DO)":;
parser(DO);
DO("do print 1; while 0;");

cerr "PT-3 parser(ANYorNum)":;
parser(ANYorNum);

cerr "PARSERTEST SENTINEL":;
stop();
